","type":"text"},{"text":"The struct keeps its memberwise initializer.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A stored property whose type isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryCodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a compile error naming it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"static method 'requireBinaryCodable(bad:)' requires that 'Foo' conform to 'BinaryCodable'","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a property ","type":"text"},{"code":"bad","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of type ","type":"text"},{"code":"Foo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Applying the macro to anything but a struct, a property with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type annotation, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"lazy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property, a destructuring pattern, a name that isn’t a non-empty string","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"literal and a version that isn’t a positive integer literal are compile errors too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store may still hold records written before an event’s stored properties changed, and reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them by name: a property removed since is skipped, an optional one added since is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the order doesn’t matter. A record that can’t be read, after a required property was added or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a property’s type changed, is dropped and reported. To keep such records, add the property as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an optional, or raise "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" and give the new shape a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"name"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text